WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.333
Local does not automatically mean safe.

00:00:02.333 --> 00:00:08.289
A server bound only to loopback is very different from one listening on a LAN interface.

00:00:08.289 --> 00:00:13.500
Once a local LLM endpoint is reachable by other devices, it needs firewall rules,

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.594
access control, logging decisions, and a clear definition of trusted clients.

00:00:17.594 --> 00:00:21.317
A load balancer that exposes several backends becomes sensitive infrastructure.

00:00:21.317 --> 00:00:25.411
Prompts can contain private documents, source code, operational details, incident notes,

00:00:25.411 --> 00:00:28.761
personal information, or secrets accidentally pasted into a request.

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:30.622
Outputs can also be sensitive.

00:00:30.622 --> 00:00:34.344
Logs may capture bodies, responses, headers, client addresses, and errors.

00:00:34.344 --> 00:00:38.067
Decide what should be logged, how long logs should remain,

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:41.044
and who can read them before expanding access.

00:00:41.044 --> 00:00:44.022
Authentication should be considered even in small environments.

00:00:44.022 --> 00:00:47.000
A lab may use a simple shared token,

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:49.978
while a team may need stronger identity-aware controls.

00:00:49.978 --> 00:00:55.189
The endpoint should not become a free compute resource for anyone on the network.

00:00:55.189 --> 00:00:58.911
Local LLM servers can consume expensive resources, process sensitive information,

00:00:58.911 --> 00:01:00.772
and interact with connected tools.

00:01:00.772 --> 00:01:04.122
TLS, binding addresses, and firewall boundaries should be intentional.

00:01:04.122 --> 00:01:07.472
Plain local traffic may be fine on one machine,

00:01:07.472 --> 00:01:10.822
while LAN traffic may require encryption depending on sensitivity.

00:01:10.822 --> 00:01:14.544
Start local-only, then expand access only with a control plan.

00:01:14.544 --> 00:01:16.778
A load balancer can centralize security,

00:01:16.778 --> 00:01:20.500
but a misconfigured gateway can expose every backend behind it.
